# /etc/inittab - NEWOS OpenRC console table (read by /sbin/openrc-init).
# Format: <id>:<runlevels>:<action>:<process>
#   sysinit   run before the runlevel chain, serially
#   respawn   restarted whenever it exits (the console shell)
#   wait      run once, waited for
#   once      run once, waited for (boot is serial; see the note below)
#   askfirst  same as wait: there is no getty to answer a prompt
# Empty runlevels means "every runlevel". Every entry runs before the respawn
# console is supervised, because the blocking wait on that console *is* the
# supervision and only one of them can be held. Only the actions above are
# implemented: NEWOS has no single-user switch, no power action and no ctrl
# allocator, so those fields are not parsed.
c1::respawn:/bin/sh --session --rc-console
